<title>FRANCE: EU agrees grain imports to Spain, Portugal.</title>
<headline>EU agrees grain imports to Spain, Portugal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday agreed to hold a tender for preferential imports of 850,000 tonnes of maize and 150,000 tonnes of sorghum to Spain, European grain officials said.</p>
<p>The tender closing date will be February 27, they said.</p>
<p>The EU's grain panel in Brussels also agreed on a tender to import 350,000 tonnes of maize to Portugal with last applications on March 13.</p>
<p>The tenders are for grain traditionally imported from the United States at lower than normal tariffs as part of a decade-old trade agreement.</p>
<p>Imports will be in calendar 1997.  </p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
